{"text": "May 15, 2014\n\nIn the interest of better managing the demand for and production of public records I\u2019d\nlike to make the following suggestions:\n\nOnce CAFI\u2019s Public Records Portal is operational, all public records requests\n(PRRs) should be made through and/or tracked by the on-line system. Chris\nPersuad is developing the Portal for the Foundation at a cost of about $1,500. The\nPortal is expected to be fully operational within the next two to three weeks. The\nPortal will allow secure access from any Internet connection and tracks the\nfollowing categories of data:\no Sending and receiving PRRs via email\no Agencies (both publicly operated agencies and vendors)\no People (contacts with various agencies and vendors)\no Contracts (both state and local vendors, including the actual contract\ndocuments)\nAll PRRs regardless of form (email, USPS, in-person, telephonic, etc.)\nAll interactions with agencies relating to a PRR\no Projects Management (these include on-going multilayered projects like\nthe School Resource Officers, School Bus Safety, Specialty License\nPlates, etc.)\n\nlomme)\n\nIn addition to the ability to track and manage PRRs the Portal will allow us to\ngenerate customized reports. For example, we can run reports that show any\nunanswered PRRs, any PRRs that are more than 30 days old, how many PRRs\nhave been made within the past week, how many denials we\u2019ve had, and how\nmany matters have been referred to attorneys for litigation. The list of reports is\nalmost limitless.\n\nUntil the Portal is operational (again, I expect this it to be on-line within two to\nthree weeks) I\u2019d like all PRRs to be sent to me for review before they go out.\nThis is something I\u2019m already doing with Cathy Zollo and Dylan Bouscher\n(\u201cDylan the Intern\u201d). My rational is that since | make so many PRRs I\u2019d like to\nhave some idea about what is being done so we don\u2019t duplicate efforts and in the\nevent that litigation unfortunately becomes necessary, I\u2019d like to be sure we have\nthe best possible set of facts.\nUntil the Portal is operational I\u2019d also like any written PRRs (email, USPS, etc.)\nto be made using the template that I provided a couple of weeks ago. This is\nsomething that has been developed and refined over the years and has been vetted\nby numerous public records litigators, the First Amendment Foundation, etc.\n\n1280 West Newport Center Drive Deerfield Beach, Florida 33442\n(888) 830-3769 / Info@CitizensAwarenessFoundation.org\nwww.CitizensAwarenessFoundation.org",
